{
  "case": "due2-duty-disjunction",
  "source": "due2-native, after the external review's R01 (docs/briefings/due2-review-2026-10-24.md): a duty whose guards and witness conditions are disjunctions (decisions/0028)",
  "classification": "odrl-core",
  "needs": [],
  "notes": "Authored for due2; no origin result. The duty's constraint is and(or(guard, guard), or(witness condition, witness condition)), each or over two different operands, so no isAnyOf rewrite removes it. odrl:purpose reads the request and odrl:payAmount the witness by the due2-core baseline (due2-profiles.md §9 #6); the policy binds ex:audience to the request and ex:paidWith to the witness. Neither or mixes a guard with a witness condition, so MixedDutyConstraint does not apply (due2-workflows.md §5.2). W1 keeps ex:pay as one atom, with two guard clauses and two witness clauses (decisions/0028). Before that decision, stage 2 made each disjunct of the full DNF a duty atom of its own, all owed: scenario 1 would then have been Pending on the copy the payment did not satisfy, scenario 2 Indeterminate on the copy that reads the absent amount, and scenario 4 Pending on two copies. The bearer is the request subject, since neither the duty nor its permission names an assignee (due2-workflows.md §5.3).",
  "prefixes": {
    "ex": "https://example.org/"
  },
